---
import Layout from "@layouts/Layout.astro";
import Container from "@components/container.astro";

// Unlisted technical overview for the Apple App Review team.
// Not linked anywhere on the site, excluded from the sitemap (astro.config.mjs),
// disallowed in robots.txt, and marked noindex/nofollow below. The URL is the
// only way in — share it only through App Store Connect review notes.
---

<Layout title="App Review — Technical Overview" noindex={true}>
  <Container>
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto mt-16 mb-24 space-y-10">
      <header class="space-y-3">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-slate-400">
          Confidential — for App Review
        </p>
        <h1 class="font-bold text-4xl text-gray-800">How Sileninja works</h1>
        <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-500">
          This page explains the technology behind Sileninja for the App Review
          team. It is unlisted and kept off our public site because it describes
          implementation details we do not publish, both to avoid helping the
          surveillance our users are protecting themselves from and to protect
          original work. Please keep the URL within Apple.
        </p>
      </header>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="font-bold text-2xl text-gray-800">What the app does</h2>
        <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-500">
          Sileninja plays a continuous, speech-shaped acoustic masking signal
          from the device speaker. The signal sits in the near-ultrasonic band
          (a configurable carrier around 19.5 kHz, range 18.5–21 kHz), above the
          range adults hear. Microphones near the phone capture this masking
          signal together with the user's voice, which substantially reduces the
          intelligibility of any speech recorded by nearby devices. All signal
          generation runs on-device in real time; no audio is recorded, stored,
          or transmitted.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="font-bold text-2xl text-gray-800">The core technology</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc list-outside pl-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-500 space-y-3">
          <li>
            <strong class="text-gray-700">Masking-signal DSP.</strong> A custom
            digital signal-processing engine synthesizes speech-like formant and
            phoneme content and single-sideband (LSB-AM) modulates it onto the
            ultrasonic carrier using a Hilbert transform. This is not a tone or
            white noise; it is structured, speech-shaped masking, which is far
            more effective against speech recognition than a static tone.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-gray-700">Speaker–microphone calibration.</strong>
            The app plays a logarithmic sweep, measures the device's speaker/mic
            response, and computes an inverse FIR filter so the emitted band is
            flat and stays inaudible across different hardware.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-gray-700">Leakage monitoring and auto-gain.</strong>
            A control loop continuously measures how much audible energy leaks
            into the human-hearing range and adjusts output gain to keep the
            signal inaudible while remaining effective.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-gray-700">Beacon detection.</strong> A separate
            detector monitors the 18–22 kHz band for ultrasonic tracking beacons
            (a KL-divergence approach in the spirit of the published SoniControl
            research) and can respond when one is found.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-gray-700">Recorder-aware behavior.</strong> The
            app detects audio interruptions and foreground recording (calls,
            voice memos) and pauses so it never interferes with the user's own
            intentional recording, then resumes afterward.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="font-bold text-2xl text-gray-800">
          Original, custom-built code
        </h2>
        <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-500">
          Sileninja is not built from a commercialized template or an app
          generation service. The DSP described above is our own work, and it is
          delivered through custom native modules we wrote specifically for this
          app:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-outside pl-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-500 space-y-2">
          <li>
            <strong class="text-gray-700">iOS:</strong> a native Swift audio
            engine built on AVAudioEngine with a real-time AVAudioSourceNode
            render callback.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-gray-700">Android:</strong> a native Kotlin
            engine using AudioTrack in streaming mode, run from a foreground
            service.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-500">
          The app does not share a codebase, SDK, or content library with any
          other app on our developer account or any third party, beyond standard
          frameworks (the React Native/Expo runtime and RevenueCat for
          subscriptions). The signal-processing engine and native audio modules
          are unique to this app.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="font-bold text-2xl text-gray-800">
          Reviewing the full functionality
        </h2>
        <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-500">
          Starting protection is a paid (Premium) feature, so on a fresh install
          the central control opens the subscription screen. To review the full
          experience, sign in on the review device with the sandbox account given
          in the App Store Connect review notes and subscribe; sandbox purchases
          are not charged. With protection active, the home screen shows live
          status and the Tuning tab exposes the strength, calibration, leakage,
          pet mode (on by default) and safety controls described above.
        </p>
      </section>

      <footer class="pt-6 border-t border-slate-200">
        <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-400">
          Questions during review: info@primarykey.solutions — we respond
          quickly and can provide a live walkthrough or a build with protection
          pre-enabled.
        </p>
      </footer>
    </div>
  </Container>
</Layout>
